# Making Your Own Ambush Datapack

Ambush encounters are plain JSON files. You do not need to build the mod, write
code, or restart the server to add one — drop a file in a datapack, run
`/reload`, and it is live.

This guide covers the **easy format**, which is what you want for almost
everything. The [advanced format](#advanced-format) at the end is only needed
for airships and other Sable-assembled structures.

---

## 1. Where files go

```text
<world>/datapacks/<your-pack>/data/<namespace>/ambushes/<id>.json
```

A minimal datapack is two things — a `pack.mcmeta` and your ambush folder:

```text
my-ambushes/
├── pack.mcmeta
└── data/
    └── myambushes/
        └── ambushes/
            └── midnight_horde.json
```

`pack.mcmeta`:

```json
{
  "pack": {
    "pack_format": 48,
    "description": "My Ambush encounters"
  }
}
```

The definition is then referred to as `myambushes:midnight_horde` — namespace
folder, then file name without `.json`.

> **Validation is strict and deliberate.** Unknown fields, unknown action types
> and out-of-range values are **rejected at `/reload`** with an error naming the
> file, rather than being silently ignored. If a definition does not show up in
> `/ambush list`, check the server log — the reason will be there.

