## 3. Presets

`preset` sets sensible defaults for trigger, timing and placement. Pick the one
closest to what you want, then override individual fields.

| Preset | What it sets up |
|---|---|
| `ground` | Default. Spawns on solid ground near the player. |
| `night` | Ground spawn, restricted to night time. |
| `land` | Ground spawn without the time restriction. |
| `water` | Spawns on/in water. |
| `sky` | Spawns above the player. |
| `air` | Airborne spawn. |
| `village` | Triggers on being near a village. |
| `outpost` | Triggers on being near a pillager outpost. |
| `structure` | Triggers on being inside a structure (see `conditions.structures`). |
| `portal` | Triggers near a nether portal. |

---

## 4. Core fields

| Field | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `format` | string | Must be `"easy"`. |
| `name` | string | Display name. |
| `description` | string | Free text for your own reference. |
| `preset` | string | See above. Defaults to `ground`. |
| `chance` | number | 0–1. Probability per check that it fires. |
| `weight` | number | Relative likelihood when several are eligible at once. |
| `cooldown_seconds` | number | Minimum gap between firings. |
| `cooldown_group` | string | Definitions sharing a group share one cooldown. |
| `distance` | number | How far from the player it spawns. |
| `check_every_seconds` | number | How often eligibility is tested. |
| `sound` | string | Sound event played on trigger. |
| `trigger` | string | `interval`, `portal`, `block_active`, `structure`, `kill`. Usually inferred from `preset`. |

### Conditions

```json
"conditions": {
  "dimensions": ["minecraft:overworld"],
  "height": { "min": 50, "max": 320 },
  "time": "night",
  "structures": ["minecraft:village_plains"]
}
```

