## 7. Unlocks — gating encounters behind progress

Encounters can stay hidden until the player has done something enough times.

```json
"unlock": {
  "progress": { "event": "kill_entity", "entity": "minecraft:skeleton", "required": 50 },
  "consume_on_success": false
},
"weight_scaling": { "per_progress": 0.5, "max": 40 }
```

With `consume_on_success: false` the unlock is permanent, and `weight` /
`weight_scaling` control how often it then appears. Inspect progress live:

```bash
/ambush admin unlocks
```

---

## 8. Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `/ambush list` | All loaded definitions. |
| `/ambush <id>` | Force-trigger one. |
| `/ambush always` | Ignore chance/cooldown while testing. |
| `/ambush clear` | Remove every active encounter, ship and placed structure. |
| `/ambush admin check <id>` | Validate a definition, including hardware requirements. |
| `/ambush admin debug` | Toggle verbose per-encounter logging. **Off by default** — turn it on before reporting a problem. |
| `/ambush admin weights` | Effective weights and chances right now. |
| `/ambush admin unlocks` | Unlock progress for the current player. |
| `/ambush admin unlockall` | Unlock everything (testing). |
| `/ambush admin spawning` | Toggle natural spawning on/off. |

